Tw 0.982 0 Td (receiver operating characteristics)Tj /T1_0 1 Tf 0.204 Tw ( \(ROC\) curve \(the unusual name )Tj 0.1008 Tw -0.982 -1.297 Td (originates from electrical engineering\). This is a plot of sensitivity \)Tj 0.0269 Tw T* (versus one minus specificity for different cut-off values. A putative )Tj 0.0504 Tw T* (plot for the diagnosis of anxiety by different cut-offs on the GAD2 )Tj 0.1309 Tw T* (questionnaire is shown in Figure 9.1. The line of equality is also )Tj 0.0786 Tw T* (shown, which is what one would expect if the test had no power )Tj 0 Tw T* (to detect disease.)Tj 0.4235 Tw 1 -1.297 Td (ROC curves are particularly useful for comparing different )Tj 0.1297 Tw -1 -1.297 Td (diagnostic plots, a plot which is consistently nearer the left-hand )Tj 0.1812 Tw T* [(side and the top is to be preferred. However)55(, further considera-)]TJ 0.0708 Tw T* (tion is beyond this book and the reader is referred to Machin and )Tj 0 Tw T* (Campbell)Tj 6.475 0 0 6.475 139.2335 216.8369 Tm (3)Tj 9.25 0 0 9.25 142.8335 213.4139 Tm ( \(Chapter 10\).)Tj /T1_2 1 Tf 11 0 0 11 100.3465 190.9139 Tm [(Diagnosis and scr)18(eening)]TJ /T1_0 1 Tf 0.0041 Tw 9.25 0 0 9.25 100.3465 172.9139 Tm (There is an important distinction between diagnosing a disease and )Tj 0.0778 Tw T* (screening for it. In the former case, there are usually some symp-)Tj 0.1707 Tw T* (toms, and so we already suspect that the patient has something )Tj 0.0601 Tw T* (wrong with them. If a test is positive we will take some action. In )Tj 0.0429 Tw T* (the latter case, there are usually no symptoms, and so if the test is )Tj 0.1009 Tw T* [(negative the person will have no further tests. Recalling Sackett\222)55(s )]TJ 0.1625 Tw T* (mnemonics SpPin and SnNout, for diagnosis we want a positive )Tj 0.0724 Tw T* [(test to rule people in, so we want a high specificity)74(. For screening )]TJ ET 
